Z||000000||Seanh||11-19-2000||10:13 PM||||I will be getting new tires during the rebuild. I was looking at Tirerack.com I am only going to be driving the car in the summer usally. Never in snow or anything, but maybe during winter and cold weather. I want some long lasting tires that perform great in handling, and smooth quiet riding. What would you reccomend I get? I want 205/60R15 front and 215/60R15 in back. Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||11-19-2000||10:29 PM||||My personal preference are BFGoodrich tires<BR>Regular T/A's for long wear excellent all weather driving. Or Comp T/A's HR4's for superb handling.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||11-19-2000||10:46 PM||||So far I've been very happy with the Bridgestone Turanza Revo H tires thatI bought recently.  They are OE tires on BMW 3 series, and are ver smooth and quiet.  They have a 50,000 mile warranty and are very good rain tires.  They are most compared to Michelin MXV tires.  Not all-out aggressive performance tires,  but those can eat you out of house and home with fast treadwear.  Good compromise tire.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||11-19-2000||10:54 PM||||I own the Comp T/A HR4's, but my first choice were the VR4's for handling. The HR4' slip progressively, but a bit early on the fronts for me. For my wife, the HR4's were a $150.00 savings.<P>What I really want are the G-Force, but I don't know if your requirement for long tread life would be satisfied.<P>BTW, there is often an opposite relationship between tread life and noise. Noise comes from a harder tread compound, which is often used to extend tread life. Hard compunds usually don't perform as well, either, especially on wet surfaces.<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||11-20-2000||09:00 AM||||Yokohama AVS intermediates!!! SUPER sticky! and quiet! good traction in the rain and just STOOOPID grip in a corner!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||11-20-2000||09:14 AM||||I love my Michelin Pilots on my 88. 205/60/r15 in front and 215/60/r15 in back. They are the best tires I have ever had. They ride real smooth and have great grip. A little expensive though. I guess because there in the Ultra High Performance All-Season category.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000006||Seanh||11-20-2000||05:59 PM||||The brands I am interested in are either Pirelli or Yokohama. I am thinking maybe the Yokohama AVID A4's, or the Perelli P6000 Sport. What do ya think?||||reg||1
